  "question": {
    "text": "A transparent block A having refractive index $\\mu=1.25$ is surrounded by another medium of refractive index $\\mu=1.0$ as shown in figure. A light ray is incident on the flat face of the block with incident angle $\\theta$ as shown in figure. What is the maximum value of $\\theta$ for which light suffers total internal reflection at the top surface of the block?<br/><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/7EQnaKMjdTVstBR849Nf3dyadKdZbzYZnVWoH2DO88A.original.fullsize.png\"/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Ybfyg",
      "text": "$\\tan ^{-1}(4 / 3)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "vWpiA",
      "text": "$\\tan ^{-1}(3 / 4)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "AeOsw",
      "text": "$\\sin ^{-1}(3 / 4)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "iiAN3",
      "text": "$\\cos ^{-1}(3 / 4)$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fEM6rHy6r1itCRQnV-3RCZCR8n1SsnKYRAM9ZsQWp9w.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{r}+\\theta_{\\mathrm{C}}=90^{\\circ} \\\\ & \\mu_1 \\sin \\theta=\\mu_2 \\sin \\mathrm{r} \\\\ & \\sin \\theta=\\frac{\\mu_2}{\\mu_1} \\sin \\left(90-\\theta_{\\mathrm{C}}\\right) \\\\ & \\sin \\theta=\\frac{\\mu_2}{\\mu_1} \\cos \\theta_{\\mathrm{C}} \\\\ & \\sin \\theta_{\\mathrm{C}}=\\frac{\\mu_1}{\\mu_2}\\end{aligned}$<br/>$\\begin{aligned} & \\sin \\theta=\\frac{\\mu_2}{\\mu_1} \\sqrt{1-\\frac{\\mu_1^2}{\\mu_2^2}} \\\\ & \\sin \\theta=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\mu_2^2-\\mu_1^2}{\\mu_1^2}}=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\frac{25}{16}-1}{1}} \\\\ & \\sin \\theta=\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ & \\theta=\\sin ^{-1}\\left(\\frac{3}{4}\\right)\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
